course: dictionary
lesson: 9946
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, so you cannot choose the right one from the spelling alone. Read the context, the words around it, and ask which meaning fits.
explain: Tart is a good example. In the rhyme, «The Knave of Hearts, he stole those tarts», tarts are small pies. If someone gives a «tart answer», tart means short and sharp, and the context shows it is unkind.
explain: Check your choice by swapping the meaning into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Tart can be a noun: a tart is an open pie with a sweet or savoury filling, like jam or fruit.
fact: «A table, with a large dish of tarts upon it» means small pastries with jam or fruit.
fact: As an adjective, tart means sour or sharp in taste, like a lemon or a green apple.
fact: A «tart answer» is short and unkind, and it shows irritation.
fact: In informal British English, «tart up» means to decorate something or make it look nicer quickly.
exercise: «The King asks what she knows about the tarts.» In this sentence, tarts means | Decorations on a hat | Short, unkind replies | *Small pies with jam or fruit | Sharp-tasting lemons
exercise: Ellie says the lemon tasted tart. What does tart mean here? | Kind and sweet | Stale and hard | *Sour or sharp in taste | Very hot
exercise: «Her tart reply made the whole class go quiet.» What does tart suggest? | Very funny | Covered in jam | Happy and cheerful | *Short and unkind
test: Mum said, «Let's tart up the cake with cream and cherries.» What does tart up mean? | To cut it into equal pieces | To cook it for a very long time | To wrap it in paper | *To decorate it or make it look nicer quickly
test: Which of these is a tart? | A kind, gentle whisper | A short, rude reply | *An open pie with a jam filling | A sour green apple
exam: In the middle of the court is «a table, with a large dish of tarts upon it»; which meaning of tart fits? | Short and unkind | To make something look nicer | Sour and sharp | *Small pies with jam or fruit
